  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mexico City L3 e-bus fleet renewal (ZEBRA Project)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The CDMX Government seeks GGGI support to perform complementary technical and financial assessments to bring the project to a ready to build (RTB) stage and secure funding for roll out. BANOBRAS, Mexico&#x2019;s largest National Development Bank, has expressed informal interest in providing debt financing for the project.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project delivers demand-led technical assistance to the Mexico City (CDMX) government to develop the country&#x2019;s first zero-emission fleet of 54 electric buses in Metrobus Line 3 (L3), benefitting at least 180,000 daily riders while avoiding the emission of 105,300 tCO2e during the project&#x2019;s life cycle.</narrative>
  </description>
